%U A179958 7021414359095808,164708060349212880,4002919021631655744
%N A179958 Number of permutations of [n] such that |p(i)-p(i-1)| >= 5 for i>1.
%C A179958 Permutations such that the absolute difference between adjacent elements is at least 5.
%C A179958 From _Seiichi Manyama_, Aug 06 2026: (Start)
%C A179958 For fixed k, let a_k(n) count permutations p of [n] with |p(i+1)-p(i)| >= k for 1 <= i < n. Inclusion-exclusion gives a_k(n) = Sum_{F} (-1)^e(F) * 2^c(F) * (n-e(F))!, where F ranges over the linear forests of the graph on [n] with edges {u,v} satisfying 0 < |u-v| < k, and e(F) and c(F) denote the numbers of edges and nontrivial components of F. Since this graph has bandwidth at most k-1, a transfer matrix whose size depends only on k computes all terms through n=N in O(N^2) exact coefficient operations. (End)
